<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Madrasa al-Shamma'iyya</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">13th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Shamma'iyya Madrasa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madrasa">Madrasa</a> al-Shamma'iyya is a college in the medina of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunis">Tunis</a>, founded by the Hafsid ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abu-zakariya-yahya-i">Abu Zakariya Yahya I</a> in the mid-13th century near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-zaytuna-mosque">Zaytuna Mosque</a>. It is generally regarded as the first madrasa in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ifriqiya">Ifriqiya</a>, and it introduced to the Hafsid lands the endowed teaching college that had spread from the Islamic east.</p></div>
